ls - list directory contents

SYNOPSIS
    ls [-alh] [file ...]

DESCRIPTION
    List directory entries in filesystem order or describe a file operand.
    With no operands, list the current directory. Directory names are
    colored on the terminal.

    -a   Include names beginning with a dot.
    -l   Show type and permissions, link count, numeric owner and group,
         size, and name.
    -h   With -l, use powers of 1024 and a unit suffix for larger sizes.

    Use -- to end option parsing. More than one operand can be specified.

EXAMPLES
    ls -alh /tmp /var

EXIT STATUS
    Zero on success, one when an operand cannot be listed, or two for
    invalid options.

SEE ALSO
    chmod(1), chown(1), stat(1), statx(2)
